# Coach speech (Finnish): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
# Always positive, never blaming. The coach says "sinä" (standard Finnish, no colloquial forms);
# Finnish has no gender, so nothing agrees with the player's or the coach's sex.
#
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level}, {opening} are always said in the nominative (no case
# forms exist for them), so each sentence puts them where the nominative fits:
#   appraisal.phase.*   nominative nouns ("avaus", "keskipeli", "loppupeli"): as the subject or
#                       predicate ("{text} sujui parhaiten", "Paras vaiheesi oli {text}") or after a colon.
#   appraisal.reason.*  an adverbial right after "Tasapeli" ("Tasapeli sopimuksella.").
#   theme.*             a verbal-noun phrase in -minen ("koko laudan katsominen ennen siirtoa"),
#                       always after a colon ("Harjoiteltavaa: {theme}.").
#   appraisal.level.*   the coach page's level name in quotation marks, after "taso" in any case:
#                       "tasolle ”Kerhopelaaja”", "tasolla ”Aloittelija”".
#   {opening:def}       the opening name as a nominative predicate ("Avaus oli {opening:def}.") or
#                       after a colon; {opening} alone as a whole sentence.
# Move numbers: the number after the noun, no ordinal: "siirrolla {n}" (at move n), "siirto {n}",
# "siirtoon {crit_no} asti" (until move n). Never a case ending on {move}, {n}, {eval}...
# Accuracy: "{acc} prosenttia" (nominative) or "{acc:gen} prosentin tarkkuudella" (count.gen says
# the number in the genitive). Counted nouns: "{n:piece_acc}" as an object, "{n:mistake}" as a
# subject or in an existential sentence ("pelissä oli 2 virhettä").

